# ── What EAS Build uploads ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Every build round uploads this tree six times — three variants, two platforms
# — and on 2 Oct 2026 EAS reported the archive at 235 MB and said so in its own
# output. Ten of that round's seventeen minutes were spent sending the same
# files again.
#
# ── This file REPLACES .gitignore, which is the trap ──────────────────────
#
# When .easignore exists, EAS stops consulting .gitignore entirely. So the
# first half of this file is a VERBATIM COPY of .gitignore, and it has to stay
# one: every rule there was written for a reason and several record an incident.
# The load-bearing one is `src/**/*.js`. A stray `tsc` run drops a .js beside
# every .ts it reads, Metro resolves .js before .ts, and a stale one wins
# silently — so dropping that single line from this file would ship code
# nobody edited. `/ios/` and `/android/` matter nearly as much: they are
# Continuous Native Generation output, EAS runs prebuild itself, and uploading
# a local copy invites it to build a stale Xcode project instead.
#
# If you change .gitignore, change the copy below to match.
#
# ── Then the second half: what a NATIVE BUILD does not read ───────────────
#
# Each directory there was checked rather than assumed — nothing under app/,
# src/, modules/ or app.config.ts imports from any of them. `data/` is the one
# worth naming: its catalogues are build-time INPUT to scripts/build-*.mjs,
# which generate modules into src/, and the app imports the generated code and
# never the JSON. The files are mentioned in comments, which is what makes a
# grep for them look alarming.
#
# `scripts/` is deliberately NOT excluded, though nothing on EAS runs it today.
# It is 1.7 MB, and the day somebody adds an `eas-build-pre-install` hook the
# failure would be a missing file on a remote builder rather than anything
# visible here. Cheap insurance against a confusing afternoon.

# ═══ VERBATIM COPY OF .gitignore — keep in step ═══════════════════════════
node_modules/
.expo/
.tmp/
.tmp-solo/
dist/
.env
*.log
# ── Anchored, and that matters ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These were `ios/` and `android/`, unanchored, which in gitignore matches a
# directory of that name AT ANY DEPTH. The intent is only the two Continuous
# Native Generation output directories at the repo root, which prebuild
# regenerates and which must never be committed.
#
# What the unanchored form also swallowed: `modules/workout-activity/ios/` —
# the entire native half of a local Expo module. Its config and its TypeScript
# were tracked, so the module looked present; the Swift module, the podspec and
# the Attributes symlink were invisible to git and were therefore never
# uploaded to EAS. Build 47 shipped the Live Activity's widget extension with
# nothing in the app able to start it: the app binary linked WidgetKit and not
# ActivityKit, and carried no symbol from the module. Found by unpacking the
# IPA, because every local build had the files on disk and worked.
#
# A leading slash anchors to the repository root. Anything called `ios` deeper
# in the tree is a source directory somebody wrote, not a build product.
/ios/
/android/

# transient edit scripts (device fs cannot rm)
.scratch*
.DS_Store
_to_delete/

dist-verify/
.fuse_hidden*
.claude/settings.local.json

# Google Play service-account key. Grants Admin on the Play developer account,
# so it never belongs in the repo — eas.json only points at it by path.
/play-service-account.json
.preflight-export/

# Signing material. Nothing here today — EAS holds the certificates on its own
# servers and none of this exists locally. These patterns are pre-emptive: the
# moment somebody picks a "download" option in `eas credentials`, a .p8 or .p12
# lands in this directory, and a private key committed once is a private key to
# be rotated.
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.keystore
*.jks
credentials.json
# The Google Play submission key, if one is ever added for Android auto-submit.
play-service-account*.json

# Staged output of scripts/import-repdb.mjs. Generated, and deliberately not
# committed: the manifest enumerates every file of a 1.8 GB licensed image
# catalogue, and the RepDB licence forbids making that catalogue available in
# bulk. A file listing is not the assets, but it is the shape of them, and it
# has no reason to be in a repository either way.
.repdb-staging/

# Compiled output must never sit beside its source. A `tsc` run without
# --outDir drops a .js next to every .ts it reads, and on 4 Sep 2026 one of
# those was committed: src/lib/offlineQueue.js, a build artifact shadowing the
# module it was built from. Metro resolves .js before .ts, so a stale one wins
# silently and the app runs code nobody edited.
src/**/*.js
app/**/*.js
src/**/*.js.map
app/**/*.js.map

$S/

# ═══ The one rule .gitignore can never give us ═══════════════════════════
#
# `.git` is 428 MB on this machine and nothing above excludes it, because
# .gitignore has no reason to: git does not ignore its own directory, it simply
# never walks it. So the verbatim copy inherits a blind spot that only exists
# once the file is used by something that is NOT git.
#
# Kept because it is correct, NOT because it was the problem — it was not, and
# the measurement says so. Two builds on 3 Oct 2026, the second with this very
# line added, both reported an archive of exactly 77.1 MB. Excluding 428 MB
# would not leave a figure unchanged to one decimal place, so `.git` was never
# in the archive to begin with.
#
# What IS established: .easignore took the archive from 235 MB to 77.1 MB, and
# the payload these rules leave behind is 1,951 files, 32.3 MB raw and 10.7 MB
# as a tar.gz. Something on the order of 45 MB of what EAS uploads is still not
# this repository's source, and there is no candidate for it here. Written down
# as an open question rather than a solved one, because the version of this
# comment that named `.git` as "the most likely remainder" was wrong within the
# hour.
.git/

# ═══ Not read by a native build ══════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Sizes are the tracked, uncompressed figures on 2 Oct 2026.
#
# NO TRAILING COMMENTS BELOW. gitignore syntax has none: the first draft of
# this file wrote `design/   # 15 MB of mockups` and the pattern became that
# whole string, matching nothing. It dropped six files out of 2,568 and looked
# exactly like a file that worked. Every comment is on its own line.

# 15 MB of HTML canvases and mockups.
design/

# 12 MB — SQL parts, setup.sql and the edge functions. All of it is deployed by
# its own tooling and none of it is bundled.
supabase/

# 3.9 MB of catalogue JSON: build-time input, see the header.
data/

# The Next.js operator console. Its own package, its own deploy.
studio-web/

# The static marketing site, deployed from Cloudflare Pages.
web/

# Planning documents and CODEMAP.md.
docs/

# Workflows run on GitHub, not on a builder.
.github/

# Repository prose. Tiny, but it is documentation for people and there is no
# reason for it to make the trip.
AUDIT-BRIEFING.md
REDESIGN-HANDOFF.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Test-only TypeScript projects. The suite does not run on a builder.
tsconfig.test.json
tsconfig.solo.json
